<!-- Battery candle, v3 sizing/colour per Ambar 2026-07-29 (see previous PNG
     design notes): body/outline/wick are shades of ONE hue per threshold,
     not a static grey. Recorded dims BEFORE this change: body 32x72,
     wicks 8x14, outline+wick static #888888, box origin (33,195).
     Applied: wick width -50% (8->4), body height +40% (72->101), outline
     and wicks recoloured to the DARK shade of whichever threshold is active
     (cyan #007888, amber #CC5800, red #CC1010), fill kept at the matching
     BRIGHT shade (#00C8DA/#FF9520/#FF4444 - the battery's own cyan, not the
     app-wide #00e5ff used elsewhere on the face). Because colour now depends
     on the threshold, wick+outline+fill all live inside the SAME Condition
     branch rather than a separate static PartDraw.

     STRUCTURAL NOTE: PartDraw's content model is DrawElement only (Rectangle/
     Ellipse/Line/Arc). Condition, PartText etc. are NOT valid PartDraw children -
     nesting them there fails silently (invalid children are dropped, no error,
     no crash), which cost a cycle earlier. Condition and PartText must be
     siblings of PartDraw, both living directly under this Group.

     Coordinate frame for every PartDraw below: box is x=48,y=200,w=32,h=129
     (moved 2026-08-05, see below) - tall enough to contain wick(14) +
     body(101) + wick(14) with NO negative
     local coordinates, since it's unconfirmed whether PartDraw clips children
     to its own declared box. Local y=14 is the body top, y=115 is the body
     bottom, throughout.

     BUG FIXED 2026-07-30 (found by Ambar - "showing blue at all power
     levels"): the threshold expressions were "[BATTERY_PERCENT] - 50" and
     "- 20", relying on Compare's non-zero=true semantic. That's only exactly
     zero when battery is precisely 50 or 20 - at every OTHER level, positive
     OR negative, the subtraction is non-zero and therefore "true", so the
     first (cyan) branch won essentially always. Never caught because testing
     only ever happened at 94-100% battery, where the cyan branch was also
     the CORRECT answer - the bug was invisible until battery actually dropped
     into the amber/red range. Fixed with real comparison operators
     (verified against Android's WFF docs: &gt;/&gt;=/&lt;/&lt;= return actual
     booleans, unlike arithmetic subtraction) - "[BATTERY_PERCENT] &gt; 50" /
     "&gt; 20". Verified on-device across all three tiers.

     MOVED 2026-08-05 (found by Ambar - "battery candle is now being cut"):
     the EUR/USD rate box (drawn in EurUsdComplicationService) was widened
     25px each side and its vertical edges thickened 5x for a bracket look,
     and its bottom (screen y~193, plus a few px more from the thick edges'
     square line caps) started overlapping this candle's old top (y=175) by
     nearly 20px. Box 1 is nearly full-bitmap-width, so there's no usable
     horizontal separation from it - only vertical separation actually clears
     it. Moved down 25 (175->200) and right 15 (33->48, cosmetic - doesn't
     affect the collision fix). This leaves only ~8px clearance from box 1
     before eating into the SESSIONS row's circles (which start at screen
     y=333) - the requested 20px clearance is NOT geometrically available at
     this candle height (129px) without shrinking the candle or accepting
     partial overlap with the session dials; flagged to Ambar rather than
     silently picking one. -->
<Group x="0" y="0" width="450" height="450" name="battery_group">
<Condition>
<Expressions>
<Expression name="batt_hi">[BATTERY_PERCENT] &gt; 50</Expression>
</Expressions>
<Compare expression="batt_hi">
<PartDraw x="48" y="215" width="32" height="129">
<Rectangle x="14" y="0" width="4" height="14"><Fill color="#ff007888"/></Rectangle>
<Rectangle x="0" y="14" width="32" height="101"><Stroke color="#ff007888" thickness="2"/></Rectangle>
<Rectangle x="14" y="115" width="4" height="14"><Fill color="#ff007888"/></Rectangle>
<Rectangle x="2" y="113" width="28" height="0">
<Transform target="height" value="97 * [BATTERY_PERCENT] / 100"/>
<Transform target="y" value="113 - (97 * [BATTERY_PERCENT] / 100)"/>
<Fill color="#ff00C8DA"/>
</Rectangle>
</PartDraw>
</Compare>
<Default>
<Condition>
<Expressions>
<Expression name="batt_mid">[BATTERY_PERCENT] &gt; 20</Expression>
</Expressions>
<Compare expression="batt_mid">
<PartDraw x="48" y="215" width="32" height="129">
<Rectangle x="14" y="0" width="4" height="14"><Fill color="#ffCC5800"/></Rectangle>
<Rectangle x="0" y="14" width="32" height="101"><Stroke color="#ffCC5800" thickness="2"/></Rectangle>
<Rectangle x="14" y="115" width="4" height="14"><Fill color="#ffCC5800"/></Rectangle>
<Rectangle x="2" y="113" width="28" height="0">
<Transform target="height" value="97 * [BATTERY_PERCENT] / 100"/>
<Transform target="y" value="113 - (97 * [BATTERY_PERCENT] / 100)"/>
<Fill color="#ffFF9520"/>
</Rectangle>
</PartDraw>
</Compare>
<Default>
<PartDraw x="48" y="215" width="32" height="129">
<Rectangle x="14" y="0" width="4" height="14"><Fill color="#ffCC1010"/></Rectangle>
<Rectangle x="0" y="14" width="32" height="101"><Stroke color="#ffCC1010" thickness="2"/></Rectangle>
<Rectangle x="14" y="115" width="4" height="14"><Fill color="#ffCC1010"/></Rectangle>
<Rectangle x="2" y="113" width="28" height="0">
<Transform target="height" value="97 * [BATTERY_PERCENT] / 100"/>
<Transform target="y" value="113 - (97 * [BATTERY_PERCENT] / 100)"/>
<Fill color="#ffFF4444"/>
</Rectangle>
</PartDraw>
</Default>
</Condition>
</Default>
</Condition>
